# graph-manager extension slot: GM_EXTENSIONS, the /ext/<name>/ proxy and the iframe page

## What to build

An admin sets `GM_EXTENSIONS="jira=http://jira:8080,other=http://10.0.0.5:9000/base"` and `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET=<shared secret>` when starting graph-manager (`apps/graph-manager`). For each extension, graph-manager then:

1. parses and checks the variable at startup in `src/server/config.ts` (a bad value, or `GM_EXTENSIONS` without `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET`, throws `ConfigError`, so startup stops with a clear message and exit code 1);
2. serves a **login-protected reverse proxy** `/ext/<name>/*` → `<url>/*` for HTTP (streamed, like the run-page proxy in `src/server/proxy.ts`) **and WebSocket**, with the same Origin check as the run-page proxy. It adds the headers `X-GM-Extension-Secret: <GM_EXTENSION_SECRET>` and `X-GM-User: admin` to every upstream request, and drops any copy of them that the browser sent;
3. exposes the extension names to the UI through a new cookie-protected `GET /api/extensions` → `{"extensions":[{"name":"jira"}]}` (never the URL or the secret);
4. shows a nav item per extension (label = the name) that links to the client route `/x/<name>`, which renders a full-height iframe of `/ext/<name>/`.

With `GM_EXTENSIONS` unset nothing appears: `GET /api/extensions` answers `{"extensions":[]}`, the nav is unchanged, `/x/<anything>` redirects to `/runs`, and `/ext/<anything>/` answers 404 (401 when logged out).

This is the spec's "graph-manager: extension slot" section (`docs/prd/automation-api.md`). The decision behind it: the extension UI is an iframe of `/ext/<name>/` that graph-manager proxies, not Module Federation, so there is no build coupling between repositories. Other work in the same run edits `src/server/auth.ts` (bearer tokens on `/api/v1`), `src/server/app.ts`, `src/web/Shell.tsx` and `src/web/App.tsx` (an Approvals nav item and page), and `src/server/store.ts`. Keep your edits in those files **additive and small** (add lines, don't reorder or reformat existing code) so the merges stay clean.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `docs/prd/automation-api.md` — section "graph-manager: extension slot" and the last acceptance criterion (the `demo` one).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts` (whole file, 129 lines) — `Config`, `BaseConfig`, `ConfigError`, the zod `envSchema` (lines 90–106) and `loadConfig` (lines 108–129). You add the two variables here.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.test.ts` (lines 1–63) — the test style for `loadConfig` (`toThrow(ConfigError)`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/proxy.ts` (whole file, 122 lines) — the run-page proxy. Mirror its `onRequest` hook (lines 71–122): path regex, trailing-slash redirect (line 79), header copy minus a `DROPPED` set (lines 13, 94–99), `reply.hijack()` and the streamed `http.request` with `x-accel-buffering: no`, 502 on upstream error, `res.on("close", () => upstream.destroy())`, `req.raw.pipe(upstream)`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/proxy.test.ts` (whole file, 177 lines) — the test to mirror: a local `http.createServer` upstream that records `seen` headers, `buildApp(testConfig(dir), { webDir: path.join(dir, "no-web"), viewCache: false })`, `app.listen({ port: 0, host: "127.0.0.1" })`, login with `fetch` to get the cookie, cleanup with `upstream.closeAllConnections()`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.ts` (lines 52–126) — `needsAuth` (lines 59–67) and `needsSameOrigin` (lines 80–85) and the `onRequest` hook (lines 119–126) that applies them. `needsSameOrigin` already returns true for **every** WebSocket upgrade (line 81), so WS Origin checking is already global; you only add `/ext/` to the path checks.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.test.ts` (lines 146–183) — the `it.each` tables for `needsAuth` and `needsSameOrigin` that you extend.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` (lines 138–168) — hook order: `authRoutes` (line 140), then `proxyRoutes` (line 142), then the feature routes; the `setNotFoundHandler` SPA fallback (lines 163–168).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/health.ts` (9 lines) — the smallest route module (`export async function xRoutes(app, ctx)`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/terminals.ts` (lines 105–137) — the only `{ websocket: true }` route: handler signature `(socket, req)`, `socket.close(4404, "...")`, `socket.on("message", ...)`, `socket.on("close", ...)`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/terminals.test.ts` (lines 1–60) — WebSocket tests with `import WebSocket from "ws"`, `ws.on("unexpected-response", (_req, r) => resolve(r.statusCode))` for refused upgrades.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/bundle-imports.test.ts` (whole file) — **server code may import only the engine package's dependencies** (`@fastify/cookie`, `@fastify/static`, `@fastify/websocket`, `commander`, `execa`, `fastify`, `ink`, `ink-spinner`, `node-pty`, `react`, `zod`, `node:*`, `graph-execution/api`). `ws` is NOT one of them (it is only a devDependency of graph-manager), so non-test server files must not import `"ws"`, not even as a type. Test files may.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts` (line 99, `STRIPPED_ENV`) and `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/runs.ts` (line 132, `delete env.GM_PASSWORD;`) — where secrets are kept out of terminals and runs. Add `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET` to both.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/test-helpers.ts` (lines 17–28) — `testConfig(dir, overrides)`; new optional `Config` fields can be passed as overrides without changing it.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.tsx` (whole file, 85 lines) — auth gate and `<Routes>` (lines 69–78).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx` (lines 42–53 `NavItem`, 65–85 the `/api/auth/info` fetch pattern, 154–185 the nav links).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/Icon.tsx` (lines 3–31 `IconName`, 32–124 `PATHS`) — add an `extension` icon.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.tsx` (line 111) and `pages/RunDetail.css` (lines 3, 21–22) — the existing full-height iframe styling to mirror.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.test.tsx` and `src/web/Shell.test.tsx` (lines 1–110) — jsdom tests with a stubbed `fetch`.
- `apps/graph-manager/README.md` (lines 71–96, "Configuration") and `TESTING.md` (lines 126–147, "graph-manager") — how to start the server for a manual check.

## Patterns to follow

**Config parsing and errors** (`src/server/config.ts`): every variable is in `envSchema` as `optional` (blank = unset); problems throw `ConfigError` with a message naming the variable. `src/server/main.ts:74-77` prints `err.message` and exits 1, and `packages/graph-execution/src/manager/start.ts:84-88` does the same for `graph-execution manager`, so a clear message is all that is needed.

```ts
// add to Config (and so BaseConfig):
/** Extension services shown in the nav and proxied at /ext/<name>/ (`GM_EXTENSIONS`). */
extensions?: Extension[];
/** Sent to every extension as X-GM-Extension-Secret (`GM_EXTENSION_SECRET`); set whenever `extensions` is. */
extensionSecret?: string;

export interface Extension {
  /** ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$ */
  name: string;
  /** http(s) origin plus an optional base path, without a trailing slash: "http://jira:8080", "http://h:9000/base" */
  url: string;
}
```

**Proxy hook** — mirror `proxy.ts:71-122` exactly for the streaming part:

```ts
reply.hijack();
const res = reply.raw;
const upstream = request({ host, port, method: req.method, path: basePath + rest + search, headers }, (up) => {
  const out: OutgoingHttpHeaders = { ...up.headers, "x-accel-buffering": "no" };
  delete out.connection;
  delete out["keep-alive"];
  res.writeHead(up.statusCode ?? 502, out);
  res.flushHeaders();
  up.pipe(res);
  up.on("error", () => res.destroy());
});
upstream.on("error", () => {
  if (!res.headersSent) {
    res.writeHead(502, { "content-type": "application/json" });
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: "the extension did not answer" }));
  } else res.destroy();
});
res.on("close", () => upstream.destroy());
req.raw.pipe(upstream);
```

**WebSocket client without importing `ws`**: the `socket` that `@fastify/websocket` passes to a `{ websocket: true }` handler is a `ws` WebSocket, so its constructor is the `ws` client class. Type it through `@fastify/websocket` (allowed by `bundle-imports.test.ts`):

```ts
import type { WebSocket } from "@fastify/websocket";
type WsClientCtor = new (url: string, protocols: string[] | undefined, opts: { headers: Record<string, string> }) => WebSocket;
const Ws = socket.constructor as unknown as WsClientCtor;
```

**Error responses**: JSON `{ error: "<lower-case message>" }` with `reply.code(n).send(...)` (see `proxy.ts:83-92`).

**Test pattern**: `proxy.test.ts` for HTTP; `routes/terminals.test.ts` for WebSocket (`new WebSocket(url, { headers: { cookie } })`, `unexpected-response` for 401/403).

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: add `Extension` (exported) and the two optional `Config` fields shown above. Add `GM_EXTENSIONS: optional` and `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET: optional` to `envSchema`. Export `parseExtensions(value: string): Extension[]`:
  - split on `,`, trim each item, skip empty items (so a trailing comma is fine);
  - each item must be `name=url` split on the **first** `=`; otherwise `` throw new ConfigError(`invalid GM_EXTENSIONS: "${item}" is not name=url`) ``;
  - the name must match `/^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$/`, else `invalid GM_EXTENSIONS: name "${name}" must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$`;
  - a repeated name: `invalid GM_EXTENSIONS: duplicate name "${name}"`;
  - the URL must parse with `new URL()`, have protocol `http:` or `https:`, and have no username, password, query or hash, else `invalid GM_EXTENSIONS: "${url}" is not an http(s) URL for ${name}`;
  - store `url` as `u.origin + u.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, "")`.
- In `loadConfig`, after the existing optional fields (line 127): when `e.GM_EXTENSIONS !== undefined`, parse it; when the list is non-empty and `e.GM_EXTENSION_SECRET` is undefined, `throw new ConfigError("GM_EXTENSIONS is set but GM_EXTENSION_SECRET is not: set GM_EXTENSION_SECRET to the secret the extension services expect")`; then set `config.extensions` and `config.extensionSecret`. When `GM_EXTENSIONS` is unset, leave both fields undefined (a lone `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET` is ignored).
- **GOTCHA**: `config.test.ts` uses `toMatchObject` and checks `"password" in c`; don't add the fields when unset, so existing assertions keep passing.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/config.test.ts`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/config.test.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: a `describe("GM_EXTENSIONS", ...)` with: two extensions parsed (`"jira=http://jira:8080, other=https://h:9000/base/"` → `[{name:"jira",url:"http://jira:8080"},{name:"other",url:"https://h:9000/base"}]`, `extensionSecret: "s"`); unset → `extensions` undefined; each error case above throws `ConfigError` with a message containing `GM_EXTENSIONS` (bad name `Jira`, `1x`, a 33-char name; `jira` without `=`; `ftp://x`; `not a url`; duplicate); `GM_EXTENSIONS` without `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET` throws a message containing `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET`.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/extensions.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: `export async function extensionRoutes(app: FastifyInstance, ctx: AppContext): Promise<void>` with three parts.
  1. `app.get("/api/extensions", async () => ({ extensions: (ctx.config.extensions ?? []).map((e) => ({ name: e.name })) }))`.
  2. An `app.addHook("onRequest", ...)` for HTTP. Split `req.url` into pathname and search like `proxy.ts:73-75`. Match `const EXT = /^\/ext\/([^/]+)(\/.*)?$/`; return when it doesn't match. **Return without doing anything when `req.headers.upgrade?.toLowerCase() === "websocket"`** (the WebSocket route below handles those). Unknown name → `reply.code(404).send({ error: "unknown extension" })`. No rest → `` reply.redirect(`${pathname}/${search}`, 302) `` (check the name is known first). Build the headers: copy `req.headers` minus `const DROPPED = new Set(["host", "origin", "referer", "cookie", "connection", "keep-alive", "proxy-connection", "upgrade", "x-gm-extension-secret", "x-gm-user"])`; then set `host` to `new URL(ext.url).host`, `x-gm-extension-secret` to `ctx.config.extensionSecret`, `x-gm-user: "admin"` and `` x-forwarded-prefix: `/ext/${name}` `` (so the extension can build absolute links). Upstream path: `new URL(ext.url).pathname.replace(/\/+$/, "") + rest + search`. Use `node:https`'s `request` for `https:` URLs and `node:http`'s for `http:`; pass `hostname`, `port` (`u.port || (https ? 443 : 80)`). Stream as in the snippet above.
  3. `app.get<{ Params: { name: string; "*": string } }>("/ext/:name/*", { websocket: true }, (socket, req) => {...})`. Unknown name → `socket.close(4404, "unknown extension")`. Upstream URL: `ext.url.replace(/^http/, "ws") + "/" + req.params["*"] + search` (search from `req.url`). Protocols: `req.headers["sec-websocket-protocol"]` split on `,` and trimmed, or `undefined`. Open `` new Ws(url, protocols, { headers: { "x-gm-extension-secret": secret, "x-gm-user": "admin", "x-forwarded-prefix": `/ext/${name}` } }) ``. Relay: client `message` `(data, isBinary)` → upstream `send(data, { binary: isBinary })`, queued until upstream `open`; upstream `message` → client the same way. Close: when one side closes, close the other with a valid code — `const code = (c: number) => (c === 1000 || (c >= 3000 && c <= 4999) ? c : 1000)` (ws throws on 1005/1006); upstream `error` (connection refused, non-101 answer) → `socket.close(1011, "the extension did not answer")`; also listen to `unexpected-response` on the upstream client and close the client with 1011. Never let an `error` event go unhandled on either socket.
- **IMPORTS**: `import http, { type OutgoingHttpHeaders } from "node:http"; import https from "node:https"; import type { FastifyInstance } from "fastify"; import type { WebSocket } from "@fastify/websocket"; import type { AppContext } from "./app.js";` — **no `ws` import**.
- **GOTCHA**: the hook runs for every request, so keep the regex check first and cheap. The auth hook (registered before) already answered 401/403 for logged-out or cross-origin requests before this hook runs, because `needsAuth`/`needsSameOrigin` will cover `/ext/` (next step).
- **GOTCHA**: register the wildcard route only once even with zero extensions (it then always closes 4404), so the module has no config-dependent branches.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run typecheck`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/auth.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: in `needsAuth` (line 59) add, before the final `return RUN_VIEW.test(pathname);`, `if (pathname === "/ext" || pathname.startsWith("/ext/")) return true;`. In `needsSameOrigin` (line 84) extend the return to `... || RUN_VIEW.test(pathname) || pathname === "/ext" || pathname.startsWith("/ext/")`. Update both doc comments to mention the extension proxy `/ext/<name>/*`.
- **GOTCHA**: another change in this run adds bearer-token handling for `/api/v1/*` to this file's hook; touch only these two functions.

