### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/extensions.test.ts`

- **IMPLEMENT**: mirror `proxy.test.ts`. `beforeEach`: start a fake upstream `http.createServer` on `127.0.0.1:0` that pushes `{ method, url, headers }` into `seen` and answers `/` with `<!doctype html><title>demo ext</title>`, echoes POST bodies at `/echo`, and answers `/base/x` for the base-path case. Attach a `new WebSocketServer({ server: upstream })` (`import WebSocket, { WebSocketServer } from "ws"` is fine in a test) that records `req.headers` and echoes `echo:<msg>`. Build the app with `` testConfig(dir, { extensions: [{ name: "demo", url: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}` }, { name: "based", url: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}/base` }], extensionSecret: "s3cret" }) ``, listen on port 0, log in with `fetch` to get the cookie. `afterEach`: close the WS server, `upstream.closeAllConnections()`, close upstream, `app.close()`, cleanup.
- Cases:
  - `GET /api/extensions` → `{ extensions: [{ name: "demo" }, { name: "based" }] }`; an app built from plain `testConfig(dir)` answers `{ extensions: [] }`.
  - `GET /ext/demo/` with the cookie → 200 and the body contains `demo ext`; the upstream saw `x-gm-extension-secret: s3cret`, `x-gm-user: admin`, `x-forwarded-prefix: /ext/demo`, `host: 127.0.0.1:<port>` and no `cookie`.
  - A browser-sent `x-gm-extension-secret: forged` and `x-gm-user: mallory` are replaced (the upstream sees `s3cret` and `admin`).
  - `GET /ext/demo?x=1` → 302 to `/ext/demo/?x=1`.
  - `GET /ext/based/x?y=1` → the upstream saw url `/base/x?y=1`.
  - POST `/ext/demo/echo` with the same-origin `origin` header streams the body through; POST with `origin: http://127.0.0.1:3000` → 403 and the upstream saw nothing.
