curl -s -b $GM_DIR/c http://127.0.0.1:7430/api/extensions                          # {"extensions":[{"name":"demo"}]}
GM_EXTENSIONS=demo=http://127.0.0.1:7431 GM_PASSWORD=pw GM_PORT=7432 GM_DATA_DIR=$GM_DIR/d2 node apps/graph-manager/dist/server/main.js; echo $?   # message naming GM_EXTENSION_SECRET, 1
GM_EXTENSIONS=Bad=http://x GM_EXTENSION_SECRET=s GM_PASSWORD=pw GM_PORT=7433 GM_DATA_DIR=$GM_DIR/d3 node apps/graph-manager/dist/server/main.js; echo $?   # invalid GM_EXTENSIONS ..., 1
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:7430/ with agent-browser, log in with `pw`: the nav shows **demo** after Reviewers; clicking it opens `/x/demo` with the upstream text in a full-height iframe. Use other ports if these are taken, and stop the servers by PID.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `GM_EXTENSIONS=demo=http://127.0.0.1:<port>` with `GM_EXTENSION_SECRET` set: the nav shows **demo**, `/x/demo` shows an iframe of `/ext/demo/`, `/ext/demo/` returns the upstream page, and the upstream receives `X-GM-Extension-Secret: <secret>` and `X-GM-User: admin` (browser-sent copies are replaced).
